    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test class, 0 failures). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that rejects creating an owner when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners, responding with **409 Conflict**. Three changes, following the existing patterns for the sibling duplicate-owner rules:\n\n1. **New exception** \u2014 `rest/advice/OwnerCityCapacityExceededException.java`, a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending city, mirroring `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` / `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException`.\n\n2. **Exception handler** \u2014 added `handleOwnerCityCapacityExceededException` to `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, mapping the exception to `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` (409) with an `errors: [\"city\"]` property in the `ProblemDetail` body.\n\n3. **Controller check** \u2014 in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, added a `rejectCityAtCapacity(owner.getCity())` call and a private helper (with a `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50` constant). It counts existing owners whose city matches case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace via the existing `normalizeForComparison` helper \u2014 the same comparison used by `nextCustomerCode` for per-city counting \u2014 and throws when the count is `>= 50`.\n\nThe provided `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fills a fresh city to exactly 50, expects the 51st to be a 409) passes, and the full suite is green.",
